.md
# Ocean waves with GLSL shaders, and XKCD-style SVG filters
In the previous post, *24K Gold, Lavender Pearls, and inked custom materials*, we explored fragment shaders on 3D plots, but barely touched vertex shaders and uniforms. This time, let's use them to turn a surface into an ocean of moving waves. We'll build the effect one step at a time, checking the geometry in Wolfram Language before moving the calculation onto the GPU.

The XKCD-style filter will come in the second part of this post and will be applied to any expression!

