  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
The definition registers a frontend symbol `MeshMod1` that returns a material factory. `MaterialShading` uses that factory when constructing the rendered mesh. Each later example follows exactly the same pattern.

Here it is on the saddle generated by `Plot3D`:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
The definition registers a frontend symbol `MeshMod1` that returns a material factory. `MaterialShading` uses that factory when constructing the rendered mesh. Each later example follows exactly the same pattern.

Here it is on the saddle generated by `Plot3D`:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Plot3D[x y, {x,-1,1}, {y,-1,1}, PlotStyle->MaterialShading[MeshMod1[]]]


