, 45.49 -36.1, 66.57 -36.22 C87.65 -36.35, 125.06 -27.8, 137.75 -24.69 C150.44 -21.58, 141.88 -18.9, 142.72 -17.56 M-0.33 0 C1.12 -3.74, -0.73 -16.45, 10.36 -22.37 C21.45 -28.28, 44.88 -35.25, 66.22 -35.49 C87.56 -35.73, 125.31 -26.86, 138.4 -23.8 C151.49 -20.74, 143.8 -18.24, 144.75 -17.14" stroke="#1e1e1e" stroke-width="2" fill="none"></path></g></g><mask></mask><g stroke-linecap="round"><g transform="translate(568.0906418368143 286.1529408140923) rotate(0 94.65220966475721 32.42468951155092)"><path d="M1.13 0.61 C4.69 9.73, 4.44 43.18, 21.48 53.83 C38.53 64.47, 75.45 65.82, 103.42 64.51 C131.4 63.19, 175.13 48.94, 189.34 45.94 M0.27 -0.12 C4.21 9.25, 6.24 44.23, 23.81 55.19 C41.39 66.15, 78.08 67.03, 105.71 65.65 C133.35 64.27, 175.47 50, 189.61 46.9" stroke="#1e1e1e" stroke-width="2" fill="none"></path></g></g><mask></mask><g stroke-linecap="round"><g transform="translate(608.6349093555662 281.377714540827) rotate(0 67.43454880224544 19.448040336330223)"><path d="M0.61 0.1 C2.95 6.68, 5.54 33.13, 15.17 39.71 C24.79 46.28, 38.45 44.3, 58.38 39.54 C78.32 34.77, 121.84 16.04, 134.78 11.11 M-0.53 -0.89 C1.55 5.34, 4.5 31.6, 14.18 38.01 C23.86 44.41, 37.42 42.35, 57.55 37.53 C77.68 32.72, 122.04 13.64, 134.97 9.11" stroke="#1e1e1e" stroke-width="2" fill="none"></path></g></g><mask></mask><g transform="translate(803.0250011108628 211.70230896495696) rotate(0 172.53985595703122 25)"><text x="0" y="0" font-family="Virgil, Segoe UI Emoji" font-size="20px" fill="#1e1e1e" text-anchor="start" style="white-space: pre;" direction="ltr" dominant-baseline="text-before-edge">Data is interpolated by rasterizer</text><text x="0" y="25" font-family="Virgil, Segoe UI Emoji" font-size="20px" fill="#1e1e1e" text-anchor="start" style="white-space: pre;" direction="ltr" dominant-baseline="text-before-edge">between the vertices on-fly</text></g><g transform="translate(602.6969211292363 143.49446701916855) rotate(351.7745663885646 28.45996856689453 12.5)"><text x="0" y="0" font-family="Virgil, Segoe UI Emoji" font-size="20px" fill="#1e1e1e" text-anchor="start" style="white-space: pre;" direction="ltr" dominant-baseline="text-before-edge">colors</text></g><g transform="translate(587.8200810956664 116.75400818933537) rotate(350.8958333017851 51.25994873046875 12.5)"><text x="0" y="0" font-family="Virgil, Segoe UI Emoji" font-size="20px" fill="#1e1e1e" text-anchor="start" style="white-space: pre;" direction="ltr" dominant-baseline="text-before-edge">screen pos</text></g><g transform="translate(672.6860515950979 171.52649985672025) rotate(15.409230435638252 35.569969177246094 12.5)"><text x="0" y="0" font-family="Virgil, Segoe UI Emoji" font-size="20px" fill="#1e1e1e" text-anchor="start" style="white-space: pre;" direction="ltr" dominant-baseline="text-before-edge">normals</text></g></svg></div>


We transform the normal with `normalMatrix`, the inverse transpose of the upper-left 3×3 part of the model-view matrix. This keeps normals perpendicular to the surface under nonuniform scaling. We normalize again in the fragment shader because interpolating unit vectors does not generally preserve their length :0

The next material adds three simple terms to the fragment shader:

- Diffuse color: `max(dot(n, lightDir), 0.0)` makes surfaces facing the light brighter - Lambert's cosine law.
- A specular highlight: the normal's alignment with the light/view half-vector produces a small bright glint.
- A Fresnel-like rim or something: `pow(1.0 - max(dot(n, viewDir), 0.0), 3.0)` highlights grazing angles.

All these directions are in camera space. The fixed `viewDir = vec3(0,0,1)` fits the default orthographic view; the light is also fixed relative to the camera. 

:::note
There is one caveat: `MeshMod3` still uses the **original** normals. The silhouette is wavy, but the highlights do not yet follow the new slopes. We'll make that mismatch visible in WL, then fix it in the final material.
:::

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.js
let THREE;

core.MeshMod3 = async (args, env) => {
  if (!THREE) {
    await interpretate.shared.THREE.load()
    THREE = interpretate.shared.THREE.THREE;
  }

  return function() {
    return new THREE.ShaderMaterial({
        name: 'MeshMod3',
        uniforms: {},
        vertexShader: `
          varying vec3 vNormals; // Interpolated camera-space normal.
          void main() {
            vec3 dir = vec3(1.0,1.0,0.0);
            float a = 0.5;
            float alpha = 3.0;
            vec3 m = a * sin(alpha * dot(position, dir)) * normalize(normal);
            // Intermediate version: lighting still uses the undeformed normal.
            vNormals = normalize(normalMatrix * normal);
            gl_Position = projectionMatrix * modelViewMatrix * vec4(position + m, 1.0);
          }
        `,      
        fragmentShader: `
          varying vec3 vNormals;
          
          void main() {
            vec3 n = normalize(vNormals);
            vec3 lightDir = normalize(vec3(1.0, 0.8, 1.0));
            vec3 viewDir = vec3(0.0, 0.0, 1.0);

            vec3 deepWater = vec3(0.2, 0.22, 0.45);
            vec3 shallowWater = vec3(0.10, 0.65, 0.80);
            float diffuse = clamp(dot(n, lightDir), 0.0, 1.0);
            vec3 waterColor = mix(deepWater, shallowWater, diffuse);
        
            vec3 halfVector = normalize(lightDir + viewDir);
            float spec = pow(max(dot(n, halfVector), 0.0), 64.0);
            vec3 specular = vec3(1.0) * spec * 0.85;
        
            float fresnel = pow(1.0 - max(dot(n, viewDir), 0.0), 3.0);
            vec3 skyColor = vec3(0.70, 0.88, 0.98);
        
            // Combine water color, sky reflection, and sun glint
            vec3 finalColor = mix(waterColor, skyColor, fresnel * 0.55) + specular;
            gl_FragColor = vec4(finalColor, 1.0); 
          }
        `,
        lights: false,
        toneMapped: false
      });    
  }
}

