%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
The JavaScript object `uniforms.time.value` supplies the GLSL declaration `uniform float time`. The `onBeforeRender` callback updates that value in seconds just before rendering. *The geometry stays on the GPU; we don't regenerate the WL plot on every frame*

The callback only runs when a frame is drawn. WLJS lets an idle scene sleep to save resources, so changing the clock alone does not keep it rendering. `SpinShow` provides camera motion and keeps visible frames coming:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
